A||||0||RFMike||Front end collision / hood release
Z||000000||RFMike||07-15-99||10:31 PM||||After what seemed like forever, I got my GT back.  It was bashed in the front in a parking lot (old post), and the hood safety bolts were engaged.  My friend with the body shop got it off with a 20 ton hydraulic puller.  I don't know how much force he applied, but when he did it, he told me to go home, that I wouldn't want to see it.  I trust him, so I did.  Point is, the hood can be removed after the safety clips and slots engage the safety studs, without drilling the hood out.  However, once you force it out, the spring clips are broken, and will not engage again.  To me, this is a good thing, although it's conceivable that the hood could go back, then forward, then back again, miss the studs, and go through the windshield.  Maybe in a multi-car pile up.  That is what the spring clips are for.  I'll take my chances.<br>Anyway, I'm back in business, with new paint on the nose and hood.  God, I didn't know Fiero withdrawal could be that bad.  
